language 0.1.0
module cli
  means
    Interaction with a program through a command line: what is named at the
    start of an execution, what the program writes back in the course of it,
    and what it reports on finishing.

entity invocation : thing
  means
    invocation: a single start of a program with everything named to it on
    the command line.

entity command : thing
  means
    command: the named piece of work an invocation asks a program to do.

entity subcommand : thing
  means
    subcommand: a command reached only through another command and narrowing
    what it does.

entity option : thing
  means
    option: a named part of an invocation, written apart from the order of
    the rest and admitting a default.

entity argument : thing
  means
    argument: a part of an invocation recognised by its place among the
    others rather than by a name.

entity output-stream : thing
  means
    output stream: a channel into which a program writes text in the course
    of an invocation.

entity exit-status : thing
  means
    exit status: the value by which a finished invocation reports its
    outcome to whoever started it.

entity usage : thing
  means
    usage: the text by which a program states the invocations it accepts.
